# ===========================================================================
# UniFlow environment
# ===========================================================================
#
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT
# -----------------
# `npm run db:start` runs a real PostgreSQL 17 server from embedded binaries
# (no Docker, no admin install). Both URLs point at it:
#
#   DATABASE_URL="postgresql://uniflow:uniflow_local_dev@127.0.0.1:55432/uniflow"
#   DIRECT_URL="postgresql://uniflow:uniflow_local_dev@127.0.0.1:55432/uniflow"
#
#
# PRODUCTION — SUPABASE
# ---------------------
# Supabase exposes two endpoints and they are NOT interchangeable:
#
#   DATABASE_URL  → the transaction-mode pooler on port 6543. Used by the app
#                   at runtime. Must carry ?pgbouncer=true so Prisma disables
#                   prepared statements, which transaction-mode pooling cannot
#                   support.
#
#   DIRECT_URL    → a direct connection on port 5432. Used by `prisma migrate`
#                   only. DDL, advisory locks and session-level state do not
#                   survive a transaction-mode pooler, so migrations run here.
#
# Take both from: Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → Database → Connection
# string. Prefer the IPv4-compatible "Session/Transaction pooler" hosts.
#
#   DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.<ref>:<pw>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=1"
#   DIRECT_URL="postgresql://postgres.<ref>:<pw>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres"
#
# Notes that matter for this schema:
#   · Tenant isolation uses `SET LOCAL app.tenant_id`, which is transaction
#     scoped and therefore safe behind the transaction-mode pooler. Session-
#     level `SET` would leak across tenants and is never used.
#   · Every RLS table is declared FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY, because the app
#     connects as the table owner on Supabase and owners bypass plain RLS.
#   · Ledger immutability is enforced by trigger, not by REVOKE, for the same
#     reason: grants do not bind a table owner.
# ===========================================================================

DATABASE_URL=
DIRECT_URL=
TEST_DATABASE_URL=

# Session signing key. Generate with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('base64url'))"
SESSION_SECRET=
